      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "GAS LANTERN (1) showed good speed off a low draw but weakened and run over late when 7th over 390m at this track in Grade 5 company. Solid record here at the distance winning eight races. Should be very hard to beat this time. LARA MOON (2) returned a better run last time, finishing in the money (22.39) at Shepparton behind Lektra Aela in a Grade 5. Has the pace to be prominent. Will give a great sight again. HARTLAND BONNIE (6) has been settling off the speed lately, finishing seventh (26.16) last time in a Grade 5 at Shepparton. Has a strong record out of this box with two wins and a minor placing from five starts. Should be about the mark. GAPING MARGIN (8) can play a role in the finish without surprising.",
